      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Creating a complex character with Hispanic roots in a high-level cartel role is a powerful way to explore real-world socio-political tensions, but it is crucial to approach this with extreme care to avoid stigmatizing or romanticizing specific ethnic groups. Instead of relying on broad \"cultural motivations\" that generalize your entire heritage, consider focusing on very specific, documented conditions in high-minority urban communities where economic despair and lack of legitimate opportunity can inadvertently channel individuals toward criminal networks. This grounded approach serves your docudrama's goal of realism by highlighting systemic failures rather than assigning ethnicity to criminality.",
